The hex images in this directory link the standard AVR runtime, version 1.8.6. It is free
software under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or any later version, whose
text is in LICENSE-runtime. Its source is not kept in this repository. packages/engine/scripts/sketches.sh
fetches it by this pin, the archive at

https://downloads.arduino.cc/cores/staging/avr-1.8.6.tar.bz2

with SHA-256 ff1d17274b5a952f172074bd36c3924336baefded0232e10982f8999c2f7c3b6. Each sketch's
source sits beside its image, and packages/engine/scripts/sketches.sh relinks every image from the sketch and
the runtime, so an image can be rebuilt against a modified runtime. A sketch that includes
Wire.h also links the runtime's Wire library, from the same archive and under the same license. The sketch sources and scripts in this
directory are under the repository's MIT or Apache-2.0 terms, and those terms permit modifying
each image and reverse engineering it to debug such modifications.

`ssd1306_power.hex` also links Adafruit SSD1306 2.5.17, under the BSD 3-clause license, and
Adafruit GFX 1.13.0, under the BSD 2-clause license. Their notices are in the `nano-oled` Block,
`blocks/nano-oled/firmware/LICENSE-ssd1306` and `LICENSE-gfx`. Adafruit_GFX.h includes the
headers of Adafruit BusIO 1.17.4, under the MIT license, and the image holds none of its code.
`packages/engine/scripts/sketches.sh` pins those three archives.

`bmp280.hex` also links Adafruit BMP280 3.0.0 and Adafruit BusIO 1.17.4, under the MIT license,
and Adafruit Unified Sensor 1.1.15, under the Apache License 2.0. Their notices are in the
`devkitc-gy-bmp280` Block, `blocks/devkitc-gy-bmp280/firmware/LICENSE-bmp280`, `LICENSE-busio`
and `LICENSE-sensor`. `packages/engine/scripts/sketches.sh` pins those three archives.

The images also hold the start-up code of the toolchain's C library, version 2.0.0, under that
library's modified BSD license, whose notice is reproduced in full in LICENSE-libc as the license
requires, and routines of the compiler's support library, under the GCC Runtime
Library Exception. Both come from the toolchain archive that packages/engine/scripts/sketches.sh pins.
